      "worked": "<strong>Show that (Z₆, +₆) is cyclic and find its generators.</strong><br>Z₆ = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, operation is addition modulo 6.<br><br><strong>Try a = 1:</strong> 1, 1+1 = 2, +1 = 3, +1 = 4, +1 = 5, +1 = 0.<br>We obtained {1,2,3,4,5,0} = all of Z₆, so <strong>1 is a generator</strong> and Z₆ is cyclic. Order of 1 = 6.<br><br><strong>Try a = 5:</strong> 5, 5+5 = 10 mod 6 = 4, +5 = 9 mod 6 = 3, +5 = 8 mod 6 = 2, +5 = 7 mod 6 = 1, +5 = 6 mod 6 = 0.<br>We obtained {5,4,3,2,1,0} = all of Z₆, so <strong>5 is also a generator</strong>.<br><br><strong>Try a = 2:</strong> 2, 4, 0 — then it repeats. Only {0,2,4}, so 2 is NOT a generator; its order is 3 and ⟨2⟩ = {0,2,4} is a subgroup.<br><strong>Try a = 3:</strong> 3, 0 — only {0,3}, order 2, ⟨3⟩ = {0,3}.<br><strong>Try a = 4:</strong> 4, 2, 0 — only {0,2,4}, order 3.<br><br><strong>Answer:</strong> Z₆ is cyclic with exactly two generators, <strong>1 and 5</strong> — the elements coprime to 6.",
