      "explain": "A map f : G → G′ between two groups is a <strong>homomorphism</strong> if it preserves the operation: <strong>f(a * b) = f(a) ∘ f(b)</strong> for all a, b ∈ G. If f is also <strong>one-one and onto</strong>, it is an <strong>isomorphism</strong>, and we write G ≅ G′ — the two groups are structurally identical.",
